<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()) - 1; (this.get(i) == null) => (this.get(i + 1) == \old(this.get(i))) || (this.get(i + 1) == \old(this.get(i + 1)));</code>

This assert statement captures the condition that for every element from the specified index to the old size minus one, the element at the next position is either null if the current element is null, or it remains unchanged.
--------------------
<code>assert index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size()) => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i+1) == (\old(this.get(i)) == null ? null : \old(this.get(i)));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size()) => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i+1)) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1)));</code>

This assert statement reflects the condition that for every element from the given index to the old size minus one, the element at the next position is either null if the current element is null, or the element at the next position is equal to the current element, provided the index is within the valid range.
